PlutoSVG 0.0.8 (https://github.com/sammycage/plutosvg, MIT: LICENSE) -- Onyx's copy
====================================================================================

The SVG renderer of NetSurf for Onyx: SVG images (content/handlers/image/onyx_svg.c) and
inline <svg> (content/handlers/html/onyx_svg_inline.c), on PlutoVG 1.3.3
(third_party/plutovg-1.3.3, unchanged). Only source/plutosvg.c and plutosvg.h are kept
(no FreeType hooks, no examples, no build files). Built by user/netsurf/Makefile
(libplutosvg.a, committed) and tools/tests/netsurf/host.mk.

The Onyx patches (each marked "Onyx:" in the source):

- <style> sheets: the text of the <style> elements read once parsed, and a CSS subset
  applied -- rules of selector lists of compound selectors (a type, *, classes, an #id)
  joined by descendant and child combinators (a selector with pseudo-classes,
  attributes, + or ~ never matches), their declarations of the presentation properties,
  "!important" dropped, at-rules skipped. The declarations go below style="" and above
  the presentation attributes, in order of specificity then of the sheets. For it: the
  class attribute kept (ATTR_CLASS), the id kept as an attribute too, style="" read
  after an element's other attributes (it wins over them), insert_attribute().
- clip-path="url(#id)": the <clipPath>'s shapes (their transforms, the element's own,
  the clipPath's transform, clipPathUnits objectBoundingBox) gathered in device space
  (render_mode_clipping in draw_shape), the canvas clipped while the element is drawn.
  An <image> is not drawn into a clip path.
- <a> drawn as a group; <switch> as its first child (no conditions read).
- url('#id') and url("#id") (quoted) in paints and clip-path.
- em, ex (of a 16 px font) and rem lengths.
- <text> and <tspan>: their characters (kept as TAG_CHARS children, between the
  tspans) drawn as glyph outlines -- the face from a font function the program sets
  (plutosvg_set_font_func: NetSurf's image/onyx_vgfont.c, the card's fonts) for
  font-family / font-weight / font-style, at font-size, from x / y / dx / dy (the first
  value of a list), text-anchor over the whole <text>; filled and stroked as a shape;
  white space collapsed, the XML entities and &#...; decoded.
- plutosvg_document_set_size(): the root viewport's size (an <img> sized by CSS: a viewBox
  fitted in the drawn box); plutosvg_document_has_view_box().

Not supported (upstream or Onyx): <textPath>, per-character x / y lists, <mask>,
<pattern>, <marker>, filters, the root's own overflow clip, XML entities in attribute
values.
